        "bean 2krx"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/harness-instances.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The four directories every instance has",
      "prov:value": "`uploads/` and `library/` are declared in this repository today and **have no\nrenderer**, which is exactly the `2krx` finding above rather than an oversight\nto be quietly tolerated.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 2krx"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/harness-instances.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where the requirement starts — bootstrap is the exception",
      "prov:value": "[The minimum `cat-harness`](cat-harness-minimum.html) carries a one-line\nadmission test from the owner's own #223 revision:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#223",
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/harness-instances.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where the requirement starts — bootstrap is the exception",
      "prov:value": "Read flatly against \"an instance renders by default\", the two cannot both\nhold. **They are not flat.** The owner settled this on 2026-09-20: the\nrequirement is a *floor that rises*, not a rule applied uniformly.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/harness-instances.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where the requirement starts — bootstrap is the exception",
      "prov:value": "In the\nowner's words, its `.json`/`.jsonld` *\"is its existence\"*",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "owner quote"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/harness-instances.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The exemption is declared data, not a special case in a checker",
      "prov:value": "— performed since 2026-09-30 by bootstrap-tools' `export-graph.ts` and typed\nby its `GraphExportSchema` (beans `n350`, `xsqm`).\nUntil that directory existed the emission discipline lived in a code comment in\n`kg-export.ts` and a YAML comment in `docs-site.yml` — which is why it was\nrediscovered rather than read, and why one of those comments still called the\ndocument *committed* four days after it stopped being.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "beans n350",
        "xsqm",
        "2026-09-30"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/harness-instances.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The exemption is declared data, not a special case in a checker",
      "prov:value": "*Tracked: `hfkl` (bootstrap's exemption and its `render/` subgraph — **done**), `ohx6`\n(`cat-harness/folio/`), `1hvo` (`cat-harness/skills/ui/theming/`), `7po1` (the workflow\nsplit this parallels).*",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "hfkl",
        "ohx6",
        "1hvo",
        "7po1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/harness-instances.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Open, and named rather than guessed",
      "prov:value": "Four questions from `yj32`, unanswered at the time of writing.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean yj32"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/harness-instances.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "KG-DS is the Knowledge Graph Data Store, and its machine is **git**",
      "prov:value": "`actorKinds: [\"system\"]`, `skills: []`, `actedUpon: true` — as written then.\nSince 2026-10-16 (owner) a role played by a mechanical actor is a real role\nwhose skills are its **contract**, `actedUpon` is retired, and this role gains\na contract skill in bootstrap. The paragraph below is the earlier reading.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "actedUpon",
        "2026-10-16"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/harness-instances.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "KG-DS is the Knowledge Graph Data Store, and its machine is **git**",
      "prov:value": "**The role carries no skills on purpose.** It holds and serves and decides\nnothing, so giving it a skill would claim it participates in a decision it does\nnot make — which is the `actedUpon` flag doing real work rather than\ndecorating.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "actedUpon"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/harness-instances.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
